  "question": {
    "text": "Let $P$ be the point $(10,-2,-1)$ and $Q$ be the foot of the perpendicular drawn from the point $R(1,7,6)$ on the line passing through the points $(2,-5,11)$ and $(-6,7,-5)$. Then the length of the line segment $P Q$ is equal to ________"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "13",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0046_8058953e492d.png\"><br />Line : $\\frac{x+6}{-8}=\\frac{y-7}{12}=\\frac{z+5}{-16}$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{\\mathrm{x}+6}{2}=\\frac{\\mathrm{y}-7}{-3}=\\frac{\\mathrm{z}+5}{4}=\\lambda \\\\\n& \\mathrm{Q}(2 \\lambda-6,7-3 \\lambda, 4 \\lambda-5) \\\\\n& \\overline{\\mathrm{QR}}(2 \\lambda-7,-3 \\lambda, 4 \\lambda-11) \\\\\n& \\overline{\\mathrm{QR}} \\cdot \\text { dr's of line }=0 \\\\\n& 4 \\lambda-14+9 \\lambda+16 \\lambda-44=0 \\\\\n& 29 \\lambda=58 \\Rightarrow \\lambda=2 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{Q}(-2,1,3) \\\\\n& \\mathrm{PQ}=\\sqrt{144+9+16}=\\sqrt{169}=13\n\\end{aligned}$"
  }
